      "y": 650.0,
      "width": 420.0,
      "scale": 1.8,
      "rotation": 0.0,
      "content": "## III. Redemption\n### We can reject and receive\n*How should Christians respond?*",
      "textStyle": {
        "size": 17.0,
        "weight": 400.0,
        "color": "#2b2116",
        "lineHeight": 1.38,
        "letterSpacing": 0.0,
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-a-card",
      "type": "shape",
      "x": -2000.0,
      "y": 650.0,
      "width": 500.0,
      "scale": 1.0,
      "rotation": 0.0,
      "content": "",
      "shapeData": {
        "kind": "rectangle",
        "fill": "#f7edcf",
        "stroke": "#b89b68",
        "strokeWidth": 2.0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-a",
      "type": "markdown",
      "x": -2000.0,
      "y": 650.0,
      "width": 440.0,
      "scale": 1.0,
      "rotation": 0.0,
      "content": "**A GOOD BUT PARTIAL ANSWER**\n### Going back to a better past isn't enough\n- Classical education and \"Judeo-Christian values\": much good, so cheer them on\n- But a heritage, not Scripture, governs it\n- So it can't critique the heritage itself",
      "textStyle": {
        "size": 17.0,
        "weight": 400.0,
        "color": "#2b2116",
        "lineHeight": 1.38,
        "letterSpacing": 0.0,
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-b-card",
      "type": "shape",
      "x": -1440.0,
      "y": 650.0,
      "width": 500.0,
      "scale": 1.0,
      "rotation": 0.0,
      "content": "",
      "shapeData": {
        "kind": "rectangle",
        "fill": "#f7edcf",
        "stroke": "#b89b68",
        "strokeWidth": 2.0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-b",
      "type": "markdown",
      "x": -1440.0,
      "y": 650.0,
      "width": 440.0,
      "scale": 1.0,
      "rotation": 0.0,
      "content": "**TWO DOCTRINES TOGETHER**\n### Antithesis plus common grace: reject and receive\n- **Antithesis**: belief and unbelief stand opposed at the root\n- **Common grace**: God's good gifts even to unbelievers\n- Together, a critical edge **and** constructive appreciation",
      "textStyle": {
        "size": 17.0,
        "weight": 400.0,
        "color": "#2b2116",
        "lineHeight": 1.38,
        "letterSpacing": 0.0,
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-d",
      "type": "markdown",
      "x": -1440.0,
      "y": 895.0,
      "width": 420.0,
      "scale": 0.45,
      "rotation": 0.0,
      "content": "### No one can hide from God\nGod's world, and even our own bodies and minds, keep speaking of him (Rom 1:19–20). Unbelief suppresses that truth but can never escape it.",
      "textStyle": {
        "size": 17.0,
        "weight": 400.0,
        "color": "#2b2116",
        "lineHeight": 1.38,
        "letterSpacing": 0.0,
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-ex-card",
      "type": "shape",
      "x": -920.0,
      "y": 650.0,
      "width": 500.0,
      "scale": 1.0,
      "rotation": 0.0,
      "content": "",
      "shapeData": {
        "kind": "rectangle",
